######################################### PRIMER ON ECCLESIARCHY SUB-FACTIONS #####################################################################
#
# The Ecclesiarchy faction in ROSIGMA consists of several parts, reflecting the unique and often self-contradictory relationship the Ministorum has
# in the wake of the Age of Apostacy and the Decree Passive. In general, the Ecclesiarchy adopts an attitude of "it's only illegal if we don't get away with it"
# attitude towards the restrictions imposed on it, and the Inquisition generally tolerates SOME level of illegality as long as the SPIRIT of the decree
# is respected, and also because it offers the Inquisition significant amounts of leverage.
#
# The "sub-factions" represented in ROSIGMA are as follows:
#
# 1) REDEMPTIONISTS
#
# This is the classic horde faction, representing both the Cult of the Redemption and other, similar cults. Poor, zealous rabble with little discipline or organization.
# Few Redemptionists have military training; they use makeshift weapons and wear little armor. Redemptionist units use "Redemptionist" as a unit name prefix.
#
# 2) SANCTIFIERS
#
# Sanctifiers are either laypeople who have joined the Frateris Militia and survived long enough to become proficient warriors, or ordained members of the Ecclesiarchy
# who have an aptitude for combat. At the low end, a member of a Sanctifier warband is at least as skilled as an Imperial Guardsman, and at
# the high end these are (or have been) trusted Inquisitoral Acolytes and retinue members, meaning they are extremely capable elites.
# Sanctifiers are essentially the Zealots from Darktide: the (unofficial) professional soldiers of the Ecclesiarchy.
#
# Sanctifier units use good quality equipment, including special weapons like meltaguns and plasma guns, and will usually have the word "Zealous" as a unit name prefix.
#
# 3) FRATERIS MILITANTS
#
# Frateris *Militants* is the unofficial nomenclature for the tiny minority of the Frateris Militia who have professional military experience. At the low end, these
# are guardsmen or PDF-level troops. At the high end, however, these are ideologically committed elite volunteers with decades of military service, using their old equipment.
# High-level Frateris Militants ride dangerously close to the limits of the Decree Passive: one of the ways the Ecclesiarchy smooths this over is by inducting former IG veterans
# into the Ecclesiarchy as lay religious brothers. Frateris Militants generally wear their old Militarium flak or Carapace armor, repainted in red and black and partly covered
# behind robes or monk vestments. High-level Frateris Militants include Kasrkin Drill Abbots, Taniths, Cadian Shock troops, and Catachans.
#
# Frateris Militants use VERY high quality Militarium gear at the top end, but lack heavy weapons and vehicles. Instead, they rely on Ecclesiarchy special units, like Miraculists.
#
# 4) OBLATIONISTS
#
# Oblationists are perhaps the most hated and feared radical sect within the Inquisition. Though obviously not part of the Ecclesiarchy itself, Oblationists acolytes are present
# in some of the Ecclesiarchy lists, being outwardly little different from any other puritan inquisitorial acolyte. At the higher levels, however, true Oblationist
# Oathed Cadres make their appearance: combining the most fanatical aspects of Inquisition monodominant ideology with the chaos sorcery, warp weaponry and heretical methods of
# the most corrupt arch-Xanthite. Oblationists have access to extremely powerful Chaos sorcery, Daemonhosts, Daemon weapons, Xeno weapons, possessed soldiers, and other profane tools.
# They are possibly the most dangerous and ruthless kind of inquisitorial warband in existence.
#
##################################################################################################################################################
# ECCLESIARCHY TENTATIVE FACTION LIST
#
# TIER 1 TROOPS: Zealots, Frateris Militia, Frateris Militia Veterans, Frateris Beastmen, Frateris Preachers, Conflagrators, Persecutors
# TIER 1 ELITES: Missionary, Salvationist, Confessor, Witchfinder Acolyte, Confessor-sergeants
# TIER 2 TROOPS: Frateris Ogryns, Frateris Shock troops, Confessor-Sergeants, Questkeepers, Pyroclasts, Sisters Oblatia, Kasrkin Drill-Abbots
# TIER 2 ELITES: Oblationist Explicator, Sister Dialogus, Miraculist, Confessor-Militant, Witchfinder Explicator, Oblationist Psyker
# TIER 3 TROOPS: Oblationist Sin-eaters, Crusaders, Oblationist Tech-priests, Banishers, Hexorcists, Oblationist Stormtroopers
# TIER 3 ELITES: Oblationist Interrogator, Oblationist Inquisitor, Cardinal, Forsaken Priest, Oblationist Possessed, Oblationist Daemonhost
# SPECIAL UNITS: Blessed Gun-Servitors, Chrono-gladiators, Arco-flagellants, Penitent Engines, Cherubim
#
##################################################################################################################################################
#
# TYPES OF WARBANDS: # (move this list to alienDeployments_ecclesiarchy.rul later.)
#
# TIER 1: SANCTIFIER PATROL 1(Conflagrators, Beastmen, Preachers, Zealots, Missionaries, Salvationists, Persecutors, Confessors)
# TIER 1: WITCHFINDER PATROL 1(Sisters of Battle, Witchfinder Acolyte, Frateris Militia, Frateris Veterans)
# TIER 1: FRATERIS CONCLAVE PATROL 1(Militia, Veterans, Beastmen, Confessors, Confessor-sergeants)
# TIER 2: FRATERIS CONCLAVE PATROL 2(Veterans, Ogryns, Shock Troops, Kasrkin Abbots, Sisters Oblatia, Sister Dialogus, Miraculists)
# TIER 2: WITCHFINDER PATROL 2 (Sisters of Battle, Questkeepers, Pyroclasts, Sisters Oblatia, Miraculists, Sisters Dialogus, Witchfinder Explicator)
# TIER 2: OBLATIONIST RETINUE 1 (Frateris Shock troops, Pyroclasts, Kasrkin Abbots, Oblationist Explicator, Oblationist Psyker, Frateris Ogryns)
# TIER 3: OBLATIONIST OATHED CADRE
# TIER 3: OBLATIONIST EXTERMINATOR CADRE
#
# NOTE: Ecclesiarchy Sororitas support comes from the Order of the Bleeding Thorn, a minor subsidiary order to the Bloody Rose.
#       This is to help differentiate Ecclesiarchy faction lists further from normal Bloody Rose/Fiery Heart OPFOR.
#
################################################################################################################################
#                                                 ##### TABLE OF CONTENTS #####
#
#
#     #1: REDEMPTIONIST SECTION
#
#     #2: FRATERIS ZEALOT SECTION
#
#     #3: FRATERIS MILITANT SECTION
#
#     #4: BLEEDING THORN SECTION
#
#     #5: OBLATIONIST SECTION
#
###############################################################################################################################

#WEAPONSETS

weaponSets:

  # CONFLAGRATORS

  # Conflagrators mainly use dual hand flamers; a minority switch one flamer out for grenades or a bolt pistol.

  - type: ECCLESIARCHY_CONFLAGRATOR_T0_SET1
    weapons: [STR_HAND_FLAMETHROWER, STR_HAND_FLAMETHROWER, STR_HAND_FLAMETHROWER_CLIP, STR_HAND_FLAMETHROWER_CLIP]
  - type: ECCLESIARCHY_CONFLAGRATOR_T0_SET2
    weapons: [STR_HAND_FLAMETHROWER, STR_HAND_FLAMETHROWER_CLIP, STR_HAND_FLAMETHROWER_CLIP, STR_PHOSPHOR_GRENADE, STR_PHOSPHOR_GRENADE, STR_KRAK_GRENADE]
